{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-001-v1","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"A","working":"Acceleration is the time derivative of velocity: a(t) = dv/dt = d/dt(2t³) = 6t². Evaluating at t = 2.0 s gives a(2.0) = 6(2.0)² = 24 m/s².","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"1.2","required_units":[1],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":9253,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":9253,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":437,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":156,"reasoningTokens":281},"totalTokens":9690,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":281,"promptTokenCount":9253,"candidatesTokenCount":156,"totalTokenCount":9690,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":9253}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":156}]},"reasoningTokens":281,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":3800,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-018-v2","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"D","working":"Work done by a one-dimensional variable force is W = ∫ F(x) dx from x = 0 to x = L. Evaluating the integral gives ∫₀ᴸ F₀(1 - x²/L²) dx = F₀[x - x³/(3L²)]₀ᴸ = F₀(L - L/3) = 2F₀L/3.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.2","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":9266,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":9266,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":450,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":173,"reasoningTokens":277},"totalTokens":9716,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":277,"promptTokenCount":9266,"candidatesTokenCount":173,"totalTokenCount":9716,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":9266}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":173}]},"reasoningTokens":277,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":5108,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-001-v1","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"A","working":"Acceleration is the time derivative of velocity: a(t) = dv/dt = d(2t³)/dt = 6t². At t = 2.0 s, a = 6(2.0)² = 24 m/s². Choice A matches.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"1.2 Displacement, Velocity, and Acceleration","required_units":[1],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":8817,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":113,"cacheReadTokens":8704},"outputTokens":517,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":148,"reasoningTokens":369},"totalTokens":9334,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":8817,"completion_tokens":517,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":8704,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":113,"total_tokens":9334,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":8704},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":369}},"reasoningTokens":369,"cachedInputTokens":8704},"ms":5225,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-021-v2","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"A","working":"The velocity is the first time derivative of position: v(t) = dx/dt = 5Dt⁴ − E. The acceleration is the derivative of velocity: a(t) = dv/dt = 20Dt³. Therefore, option A is correct.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"1.2","required_units":[1],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":9249,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":9249,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":522,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":149,"reasoningTokens":373},"totalTokens":9771,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":373,"promptTokenCount":9249,"candidatesTokenCount":149,"totalTokenCount":9771,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":9249}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":149}]},"reasoningTokens":373,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":5892,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-021-v2","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"A","working":"Differentiate position once: v(t) = 5Dt⁴ − E. Differentiate again: a(t) = 20Dt³. So A is correct. B is velocity; C and D are incorrect.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"1.2 Displacement, Velocity, and Acceleration","required_units":[1],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":8819,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":115,"cacheReadTokens":8704},"outputTokens":721,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":134,"reasoningTokens":587},"totalTokens":9540,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":8819,"completion_tokens":721,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":8704,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":115,"total_tokens":9540,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":8704},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":587}},"reasoningTokens":587,"cachedInputTokens":8704},"ms":7213,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-025-v3","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"D","working":"Using Newton's second law, m(dv/dt) = -bv or m(dv/dx) = -b. Integrating from v = v_0 to v = 0 gives m(0 - v_0) = -b*x, which yields x = m*v_0 / b = (5.0 kg * 8.0 m/s) / (2.0 kg/s) = 20 m.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"2.9","required_units":[1,2],"difficulty":"Medium"},"usage":{"inputTokens":9269,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":9269,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":697,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":192,"reasoningTokens":505},"totalTokens":9966,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":505,"promptTokenCount":9269,"candidatesTokenCount":192,"totalTokenCount":9966,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":9269}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":192}]},"reasoningTokens":505,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":5316,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-018-v2","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"D","working":"Use the integral definition of work: W = ∫ F(x) dx from 0 to L. W = F₀∫(1 − x²/L²)dx = F₀[x − x³/(3L²)] from 0 to L = F₀(L − L/3) = 2F₀L/3.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.2 Work","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":8844,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":12,"cacheReadTokens":8832},"outputTokens":1076,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":155,"reasoningTokens":921},"totalTokens":9920,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":8844,"completion_tokens":1076,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":8832,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":12,"total_tokens":9920,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":8832},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":921}},"reasoningTokens":921,"cachedInputTokens":8832},"ms":10874,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-018-v3","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"B","working":"Work is W = ∫ F dx. Here W = ∫₀^∞ F₀L³/(x+L)³ dx. Substitute u = x+L: W = F₀L³ ∫_L^∞ u⁻³ du = F₀L³ [ -1/(2u²) ]_L^∞ = F₀L³ (0 + 1/(2L²)) = F₀L/2.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.2 Work","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Medium"},"usage":{"inputTokens":8834,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":2,"cacheReadTokens":8832},"outputTokens":642,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":176,"reasoningTokens":466},"totalTokens":9476,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":8834,"completion_tokens":642,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":8832,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":2,"total_tokens":9476,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":8832},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":466}},"reasoningTokens":466,"cachedInputTokens":8832},"ms":6620,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-018-v3","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"B","working":"Work is the integral of force over displacement: W = ∫₀^∞ F₀L³/(x + L)³ dx. Evaluating gives F₀L³ [-1 / (2(x + L)²)] from 0 to ∞ = F₀L³ [0 - (-1/(2L²))] = F₀L/2.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.2","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Medium"},"usage":{"inputTokens":9257,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":9257,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":643,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":165,"reasoningTokens":478},"totalTokens":9900,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":478,"promptTokenCount":9257,"candidatesTokenCount":165,"totalTokenCount":9900,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":9257}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":165}]},"reasoningTokens":478,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":8622,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-026-v3","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"C","working":"The net force is centripetal: F_net = m*a_c = m*(4*pi^2*r / T^2). Substituting m = 4.0 kg, r = 1.5 m, and T = 0.50 s gives F_net = 4.0 * (4 * pi^2 * 1.5) / (0.50)^2 = 24*pi^2 * 4.0 ≈ 947 N ≈ 950 N, directed toward the center of the circle.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"2.10","required_units":[2],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":9285,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":9285,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":956,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":217,"reasoningTokens":739},"totalTokens":10241,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":739,"promptTokenCount":9285,"candidatesTokenCount":217,"totalTokenCount":10241,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":9285}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":217}]},"reasoningTokens":739,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":7627,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-027-v1","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"B","working":"Work done by a variable one-dimensional force is given by W = ∫ F(x) dx from x₁ to x₂. Here, W = ∫₁³ (3.0x²) dx = [x³]₁³ = 3³ - 1³ = 27 - 1 = 26 J.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.2","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":9267,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":9267,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":523,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":163,"reasoningTokens":360},"totalTokens":9790,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":360,"promptTokenCount":9267,"candidatesTokenCount":163,"totalTokenCount":9790,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":9267}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":163}]},"reasoningTokens":360,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":4939,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-028-v3","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"D","working":"The relationship between force and potential energy in one dimension is F_x = -dU/dx. Given U(x) = 4.0 x^(-2), taking the derivative yields dU/dx = -8.0 x^(-3), so F_x = +8.0/x^3. Evaluating at x = 0.50 m gives F_x = 8.0 / (0.50)^3 = 8.0 / 0.125 = +64 N, which is in the +x direction.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.3","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Medium"},"usage":{"inputTokens":9278,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":9278,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":640,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":213,"reasoningTokens":427},"totalTokens":9918,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":427,"promptTokenCount":9278,"candidatesTokenCount":213,"totalTokenCount":9918,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":9278}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":213}]},"reasoningTokens":427,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":4857,"error":""}
